    "character": "惟",
    "aliases": [],
    "unicode": "U+60DF",
    "title_english": "惟: thinking and grammaticalization",
    "summary_english": "惟 is a heart-radical phonetic compound whose original meaning is to think. Through loan use it developed adverbial, conjunctive, and modal functions, in a complex history shared with 唯 and 维.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "惟",
      "pronunciation": "wéi喻纽、微部；以纽、脂韵、以追切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《甲金篆》735页",
        "《说文》218页",
        "《隶辨》50页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "形声字。从心，隹声。战国金文从“心”﹑“唯”声；小篆为左“心”﹑右“隹”；隶楷文字由小篆演变而来，写作“惟”。本义为思考。\n《说文》：“惟，凡思也。”\n《诗·大雅·生民》：“载谋载惟，取萧祭脂。”\n（筹划思考祭礼事，取来香蒿烧油脂）\n郑玄笺：“惟，思也。”\n后因读音相同的关系，假借用作副词，指“单单﹑只有”或“又﹑还”；又假借用作连词，可以表示并列﹑顺承﹑让步等关系；还假借用作语气助词，可用于句首，也可用于句中。从字用层面上看，“惟﹑唯﹑维”的纠缠很值得关注。例如“唯一”“惟一”，“思维”“思惟”，就很纠结。从根源上说，“惟”是“凡思”，故从“心”；“唯”是“唯诺”，故从“口”；“维”是“维系”，故从“系”。至于用为语助，则早期仅作“隹”，借鸟形之字而为之，或者竟是取其鸟鸣声的模拟。其后加“口”为“唯”，渐又混用“惟”“维”。另外，“誰”\n（谁）\n字也是“隹”“唯”系列语法化发展的结果，这是我们的一个新的发现。大致情形是，“唯”的聚焦语气用法转为疑问语气时，导致了疑问代词“谁”的出现，专司特指问。\n（郭小武 叶青）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "惟 consists of 心 and 隹 as phonetic. Warring States bronze forms use 心 with 唯 as the phonetic; Small Seal has 心 on the left and 隹 on the right, and clerical and regular script developed from it as 惟. Its original sense is thinking. 《说文》 says, “惟，凡思也。” 《诗·大雅·生民》 says, “载谋载惟，取萧祭脂。”—planning and considering the ritual, then taking fragrant mugwort and burning fat. Zheng Xuan’s commentary says, “惟，思也。”",
        "Because of shared pronunciation, 惟 was borrowed as an adverb meaning “only” or “also, still”; as a conjunction expressing coordination, succession, or concession; and as a modal particle at the beginning or middle of a sentence. The entanglement of 惟, 唯, and 维 at the level of actual writing deserves attention: compare 唯一 and 惟一, or 思维 and 思惟. At root, 惟 is “thinking in all cases,” hence 心; 唯 is assent, hence 口; 维 is binding or tying, hence 系. In particle use the early form was only 隹, borrowing the bird graph, perhaps even imitating birdsong; 口 was later added to make 唯, and 惟 and 维 gradually mixed with it. The character 誰\n（谁）\n is also said to result from the grammaticalization of the 隹/唯 series. This is presented as a new finding: when 唯’s focusing modal use shifted to an interrogative one, it produced the specific-question pronoun 谁."
      ]
    },
