    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "情",
      "pronunciation": "qíng从纽、耕部；从纽、清韵、疾盈切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《说文》217页",
        "《甲金篆》727页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "形声字。从心，青声。小篆为左“心”﹑右“青”；汉代简帛文字或作左“心”﹑右“青”，或作上“青”﹑下“心”；隶楷文字与小篆一脉相承，写作“情”。本义指感情﹑情绪。\n《说文》：“情，人之阴气有欲者。”\n徐灏注笺：“发于本心谓之情。”\n《礼记·礼运》：“何谓人情？喜﹑怒﹑哀﹑惧﹑爱﹑恶﹑欲，七者弗学而能。”\n由感情引申为本性﹑情欲﹑爱情﹑意愿﹑欲望﹑情趣﹑私情﹑情面﹑常情﹑实情等义，又由实情引申为情况﹑情形等。\n（郭小武 叶青）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "A phonosemantic character, from 心 ‘heart’ with 青 as phonetic. The small seal form has 心 on the left and 青 on the right. Han bamboo and silk texts may have this arrangement or 青 above and 心 below; clerical and regular script continue the small-seal line and write 情. Its original meaning is ‘feeling’ or ‘emotion’. 《说文》 says: 情，人之阴气有欲者。 Xu Hao’s note says: 发于本心谓之情。 《礼记·礼运》 reads: 何谓人情？喜﹑怒﹑哀﹑惧﹑爱﹑恶﹑欲，七者弗学而能。 From feelings it was extended to natural disposition, desire, sexual desire, love, intention, wish, interest, private feeling, personal consideration, ordinary human feeling, and the true state of affairs; from the latter it further developed the senses ‘situation’ and ‘circumstance’. (Guo Xiaowu; Ye Qing)"
      ]
    },
