    "character": "代",
    "aliases": [],
    "unicode": "U+4EE3",
    "title_english": "代: succession and replacement",
    "summary_english": "代 is a semantic–phonetic character formed from 人 and 弋. Its original meaning is replacement or succession.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "代",
      "pronunciation": "dài定纽、职部；定纽、代韵、徒耐切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《甲金篆》552页",
        "《说文》165页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "形声字。从人，弋声。本义是更替。\n《说文》：“代，更也。”\n（董莲池）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "代 combines 人 with the phonetic 弋. Its basic meaning is to replace one thing or person with another, or to succeed in turn. 《说文》 defines it succinctly: “代，更也。”"
      ]
    },
