    "unicode": "U+8981",
    "title_english": "要: an uncertain structure and the historical waist",
    "summary_english": "要 has an uncertain graphic structure. The Small Seal form discussed by 《说文》 has no known close predecessor in Western Zhou through Han sources, while the modern form derives from the ancient form of 要, which was graphically identical with ancient 娄.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "要",
      "pronunciation": "yāo影纽、宵部；影纽、宵韵、於宵切。\nyào影纽、宵部；影纽、笑韵、於笑切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《金文编》167页",
        "《上海博物馆藏战国楚竹书（一）·性情论》第14号简",
        "《说文》60页",
        "《汉印徵》卷3，13页",
        "《睡甲》39页",
        "《篆隶表》185页",
        "《汉语字形表》104页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "构形不明。《说文》以“要”为“腰”的本字：“要，身中也，象人要自𦥑之形。从𦥑，交省声。”这是就《说文》小篆字形立说。《说文》小篆“要”字来源不明，西周﹑战国﹑秦﹑汉均未见与其形体相近的“要”字。现在楷书的“要”也不是由小篆隶定而来，而是源自《说文》古文的“要”。《说文》古文“要”与“娄”字的古文相同，致使古文字中的“要”﹑“娄”莫辨。现在可以从辞例上确认的“要”字最早见于战国楚简，显然是《说文》古文所本。秦﹑汉的古隶和今隶也都是由这一形体演变而来。从这个字形下部从女﹑从交叉两手来看，《说文》以其为“腰”的本字或许是可信的。\n（李守奎）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "The structure of 要 is uncertain. 《说文》 treats 要 as the original character for 腰: “要，身中也，象人要自𦥑之形。从𦥑，交省声。” This analysis addresses the Small Seal form, whose source remains unknown: no close form is known from Western Zhou, Warring States, Qin, or Han writing. Modern regular-script 要 also does not derive by clerical transformation from that Small Seal form; it derives from the ancient form of 要 recorded in 《说文》. That ancient form is identical with the ancient form of 娄, making 要 and 娄 difficult to distinguish in early materials. The earliest securely identified 要 occurs in Warring States Chu slips and evidently provides the basis for the 《说文》 ancient form. Qin and Han ancient clerical and standard clerical writing descend from it. Since its lower part combines 女 with crossed hands, 《说文》’s identification of the word as the original 腰 may be credible."
      ]
    },
