    "unicode": "U+88AB",
    "title_english": "被 — bedding, covering, and undergoing",
    "summary_english": "A phonetic compound from 衣 and 皮, 被 originally denoted bedding or a quilt. The image of a quilt laid over the body gave rise to surface, covering, applying, and undergoing.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "被",
      "pronunciation": "bèi並纽、歌部；並纽、纸韵、皮彼切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《甲金篆》585页",
        "《说文》172页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "形声字。\n《说文》：“被，寝衣也。从衣，皮声。”\n寝衣指被子，此即其本义。《论语·乡党》“必有寝衣，长一身有半。”是其用。被子是盖在人身上的，引申而有表面﹑覆盖﹑施加﹑遭受诸义。字形以战国所见为最早，有左形右声者，有外形内声者。秦时起，固定为左形右声结构，汉代隶变发生之后，意符“衣”变作“衤”。\n（董莲池）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "A phonetic compound. 《说文》：“被，寝衣也。从衣，皮声。” 寝衣 means bedding or a quilt, which is the original meaning. 《论语·乡党》 says “必有寝衣，长一身有半”, an example of this use. Because a quilt covers a person, 被 developed the meanings surface, covering, applying, and undergoing.",
        "The earliest forms appear in Warring-States writing, with both left-semantic/right-phonetic and enclosing-semantic/internal-phonetic layouts. From Qin onward the left-semantic/right-phonetic structure became fixed. After clerical transformation, the semantic component 衣 became 衤. （董莲池）"
      ]
    },
