    "title_english": "雅 — correct speech, elegance, and customary practice",
    "summary_english": "A phonetic compound from 隹 and 牙, 雅 developed from an early graph with 牙 as its source and phonetic. It was borrowed for ‘correct’ and ‘standard’, then extended to elegance, exemplary closeness to a norm, ordinary practice, a child, and the central plains.",
