    "unicode": "U+7384",
    "title_english": "玄 — reddish black, depth, and mystery",
    "summary_english": "A differentiated variant of the borrowed graph 幺, 玄 originally denotes a reddish-black colour. The colour’s indeterminate depth yielded the senses remote, profound, marvelous, and in modern use deceptive or unreliable.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "玄",
      "pronunciation": "xuán匣纽、真部；匣纽、先韵、胡涓切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《金文编》272页",
        "《金文编》268页",
        "《郭店》73页",
        "《说文》84页",
        "《睡甲》57页",
        "《马王堆》153页",
        "《甲金篆》253页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "幺之借形变体分化字。本作幺，表物体之色度\n（参见“幺”字条）\n。晚周以后字形上部追加圆点状区别符号而别出，后世再线化为一横而为秦篆所本。“玄”字本义指赤黑色。\n《说文》：“玄，黑而有赤色者为玄。”\n《诗·小雅·何草不黄》：“何草不玄。”\n郑玄笺：“玄，赤黑色。”\n吉日壬午剑“玄镠”，即指赤黑色的美金。因赤黑色不是单纯色，在色阶上具有一定的模糊性﹑隐晦性，所以“玄”可引申为幽远义。\n《说文》：“玄，幽远也。”\n《楚辞·九章·惜往日》：“临沅湘之玄渊兮，遂自忍而沈流。”\n也可引申为奥妙义。\n《玉篇·玄部》：“妙也。”\n郭店楚墓竹简《老子甲》8：“长古之善为士者，必非\n（微）\n溺\n（妙）\n玄达，深不可志\n（识）\n。”\n《老子》第一章：“玄之又玄，众妙之门。”\n又可引申为虚伪﹑不可靠义，如这话太玄了。\n（齐航福）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "玄 is a differentiated variant of the borrowed-form graph 幺, which originally expressed an object’s degree of colour, as discussed under 幺. From the late Zhou onward, a dot-like distinguishing mark was added above it; later it became a horizontal stroke, the basis of the Qin seal form. The original meaning is reddish black. 《说文》：“玄，黑而有赤色者为玄。” 《诗·小雅·何草不黄》：“何草不玄。” Zheng Xuan glosses: “玄，赤黑色。” The phrase 玄镠 on the Ji ri renwu sword refers to beautiful metal of reddish-black colour.",
        "Because reddish black is not a simple colour and has an element of indistinctness and concealment on a colour scale, 玄 developed the sense remote and profound. 《说文》：“玄，幽远也。” 《楚辞·九章·惜往日》：“临沅湘之玄渊兮，遂自忍而沈流。” It also means marvelous. 《玉篇·玄部》：“妙也。” The Guodian Chu bamboo-strip 《老子甲》8 reads: “长古之善为士者，必非（微）溺（妙）玄达，深不可志（识）。” Here 非 glosses 微, 溺 glosses 妙, and 志 glosses 识. 《老子》第一章 says: “玄之又玄，众妙之门。” In modern usage 玄 can also mean false or unreliable, as in saying that a claim is too 玄. （齐航福）"
      ]
    },
