    "unicode": "U+5E2B",
    "title_english": "師: troops, master, and teacher",
    "summary_english": "師 is related to a military formation and later a skilled leader or teacher. 师 is the simplified form.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "師",
      "entry_form": "師",
      "related_headwords": [
        "师"
      ],
      "pronunciation": "",
      "bibliography": [
        "（原文为反书）﹑6–12﹑15《汉语字形表》233～234页",
        "《说文》127页",
        "《睡甲》91页",
        "《篆隶表》402页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "“師”字，商代甲骨文作，构形不明，隶定作“𠂤”\n（参见𠂤部“𠂤（duī）”字条）\n。西周金文或作“𠂤”，或加“帀”旁作“師”，或省“𠂤”旁作“帀”\n（参见上“帀2”字条）\n。春秋战国及秦汉文字承袭西周金文，亦作“師”﹑“帀”二体\n（字形15将“𠂤”横书置于“帀”旁之上，字形19即此形之讹）\n。古代军队编制单位，二千五百人为一师。\n《说文》：“師，二千五百人为師。”\n《周礼·地官·小司徒》：“五人为伍，五伍为两，四两为卒，五卒为旅，五旅为師，五師为军。”\n泛指军队。\n禹鼎：“王乃命西六𠂤\n（師）\n﹑殷八𠂤\n（師）\n。”\n《左传·僖公四年》：“齐侯以诸侯之師侵蔡。”\n鄂君启舟节：“大司马昭阳败晋帀\n（師）\n于襄陵之岁。”\n又指驻扎军队。\n《左传·僖公二十五年》：“秦伯師于河上。”\n引申指众，众人。\n《诗·大雅·韩奕》：“薄彼韩城，燕師所完。”\n毛传：“師，众也。”\n又为官名。如太师﹑师氏﹑乐师等。又指精通某种技艺的人。\n《孟子·告子上》：“今有场師。”\n赵岐注：“场師，治场圃者。”\n又指先生，老师。\n《论语·述而》：“三人行，必有我師焉。”\n《玉篇·帀部》：“師，教人以道者之称也。”\n“師”字在汉代还有过一个假借义。\n《汉书·西域传》：“\n（乌弋山离）\n有桃拔﹑師子﹑犀牛。”\n这种用法的“師”，后来加“犬”旁写作“獅”。《说文》无“獅”字。\n《玉篇·犬部》：“獅，音師，猛兽也。”\n新中国成立后，“師”简化为“师”，“獅”类推简化为“狮”。\n（冀小军）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "requested_character": "師",
      "redirects": [],
      "explanation_english": [
        "師 is historically associated with organized troops and a military command. 《说文》 says “師，二千五百人为师,” defining it as an army unit. Early forms show a banner-like element that evokes a formation. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《周礼·地官·小司徒》. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《左传·僖公二十五年》. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《孟子·告子上》. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《玉篇·帀部》. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《玉篇·犬部》. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「五人为伍，五伍为两，四两为卒，五卒为旅，五旅为師，五師为军。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「齐侯以诸侯之師侵蔡。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「秦伯師于河上。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「師，众也。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「场師，治场圃者。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「師，教人以道者之称也。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「獅，音師，猛兽也。」.",
        "From the commander or leader of an army came the senses master, teacher, specialist, model, and religious preceptor. It also remains a collective term for troops. 师 is the modern simplified form. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《左传·僖公四年》. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《诗·大雅·韩奕》. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《论语·述而》. Classical evidence for military formations, commanders, and teachers occurs in 《汉书·西域传》. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「師，二千五百人为師。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「王乃命西六𠂤（師）﹑殷八𠂤（師）。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「大司马昭阳败晋帀（師）于襄陵之岁。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「薄彼韩城，燕師所完。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「今有场師。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「三人行，必有我師焉。」. For military formations, commanders, and teachers, the text states 「（乌弋山离）有桃拔﹑師子﹑犀牛。」."
      ]
    },
