    "summary_english": "爾 is an ancient graph whose rare original meaning concerned an interlaced window lattice. It was overwhelmingly borrowed for the second-person pronoun and related particles; 尔 is simplified.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "爾",
      "entry_form": "爾",
      "related_headwords": [
        "尔"
      ],
      "pronunciation": "",
      "bibliography": [
        "《汉语字形表》130页",
        "《金文编》231页",
        "《四声韵》37页",
        "《战文编》214页",
        "《说文》70页",
        "《隶辨》337～338页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "初为象形字。殷商甲骨文像三足的络丝架，上有锐头，中有器身，下有竖足，为“𪱾”\n（nǐ，络丝𪱾）\n之初文。到西周春秋时，锐头下各衍出一点，遂成“尔”字，且由原本的象形构件转化为表音构件，原来的象形字也就演进为形声字，尔与爾同为日纽脂部。此时，器足消失，与器身整合为一，器身上用多少不等﹑方向不同的线条表缠绕之丝。到战国时，繁体作从人﹑爾声，简体作。至《说文》将其整理作从冂﹑从㸚﹑尔声，属于理据重构。其实冂与㸚是器身与器足的演化，尔声是器首的演化，本形声字出自象形字的讹变。隶变后楷书作爾，简化字作尔。尔与爾原本同为一字，后由爾分化出尔。简化时以尔代爾是以简代繁，也是爾与尔复归为一。《说文》本义为“丽尔”，即“丽𫷹”，窗棂交错，格格相连。此义罕用，多用假借义。人名。\n《殷虚书契前编》7.42.2：“丁丑卜，宾贞：尔得？王󶐻曰：其得。”\n方国名。\n《殷虚文字缀合》282：“癸酉卜，𣪊贞：令多奠﹑依﹑尔𩫖\n（墉）\n？”\n第二人称代词，你。\n齐侯壶：“万年无疆，用御\n（治理）\n尔事。”\n马王堆汉墓帛书《五行篇》：“毋\n（贰）\n尔心。”\n华盛貌。\n《诗·小雅·采薇》：“彼尔维何，维常之华。”\n墙盘：“剌且\n（祖）\n文考弋𫴡受墙尔𪓐。”\n（烈祖文考特授予墙繁茂兴盛）\n此义后写作“薾”。以上读ěr。借用作“沵”，满﹑众，读mǐ。通“迩”，近。\n《诗·大雅·行苇》：“戚戚兄弟，莫远具尔。”\n孔颖达疏：“迩是近义。”\n通“弥”，更加。\n郭店楚简《老子》甲本：“夫\n（天）\n下多\n（忌）\n韦\n（讳）\n，民尔畔\n（叛）\n。”\n参“尔”字条。\n（张标）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "requested_character": "爾",
      "redirects": [],
      "explanation_english": [
        "The received analysis of 爾 as a complex semantic–phonetic structure is treated as a later reconstruction: its ancient form arose through transformation of an original pictograph, likely an object with body, feet, and head. 《说文》 gives the rare original sense “丽尔,” an interlaced window lattice. 爾 and 尔 were originally one graph before differentiation; modern simplification reunified them in 尔. For the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, a classical use occurs in 《殷虚书契前编》. For the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, a classical use occurs in 《五行篇》. For the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, a classical use occurs in 《诗·大雅·行苇》. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「丁丑卜，宾贞：尔得？王󶐻曰：其得。」. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「万年无疆，用御（治理）尔事。」. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「彼尔维何，维常之华。」. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「戚戚兄弟，莫远具尔。」. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「夫（天）下多（忌）韦（讳），民尔畔（叛）。」.",
        "The common uses are ‘you,’ as in 齐侯壶 “用御尔事,” and an intensifying or manner particle ‘thus.’ It can mean flourishing, be borrowed for 沵 ‘full/many,’ for 迩 ‘near,’ and for 弥 ‘all the more.’ Ancient oracle texts also use it in personal and regional names. For the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, a classical use occurs in 《殷虚文字缀合》. For the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, a classical use occurs in 《诗·小雅·采薇》. For the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, a classical use occurs in 《老子》. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「癸酉卜，𣪊贞：令多奠﹑依﹑尔𩫖（墉）？」. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「毋（贰）尔心。」. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「剌且（祖）文考弋𫴡受墙尔𪓐。」. To show the pronoun ‘you,’ flourishing appearance, proximity, and intensification, the text says 「迩是近义。」."
      ]
    },
