      "explanation_original": "形声字。从貝，臤声。“臤”乃“掔”\n（音qiān）\n之初文，本义是除去\n（《庄子·徐无鬼》：“君将黜耆欲，掔好恶，则耳目病矣。”）\n。商代金文作，从又﹑从臣，像以手指抉人之目。西周金文作\n（字形3“賢”字所从）\n，手指与目形分离，造字意图已不明显；或省作\n（字形2）\n，字义亦不甚显豁。战国文字承袭西周金文，亦有﹑二形\n（字形5﹑6）\n；或将二者组合，写作\n（字形8）\n，则像眼球已被抉出\n（战国文字中，“臤”所从之“又”上面多有一笔或两笔，即此形之变）\n。古文字多借“臤”为“賢”。\n《说文·臤部》：“臤，古文以为賢字。”\n柞伯簋：“王迟赤金十反\n（钣）\n。王曰：‘小子﹑小臣，敬又臤\n（賢）\n隻\n（获）\n则取。’”\n（迟：读为“陈”，陈列。臤：字形2。\n《小尔雅·广诂》：“賢，多也。”\n此句的完整意思是：王陈列赤金十钣作为奖品，说：“小子﹑小臣，恭敬而射中多的可得到这些奖品。”）\n郭店楚墓竹简《唐虞之道》：“尧舜之行，爱亲尊臤\n（賢）\n。”\n（字形6）\n又《语丛四》：“臤\n（賢）\n人不在侧，是谓迷惑。”\n（字形8）\n汉校官碑：“亲臤\n（賢）\n宝知\n（智）\n。”\n（字形17）\n《说文》：“賢，多才也。”\n《周礼·地官·乡大夫》：“兴賢者能者。”\n郑玄注：“賢者，有德行者。”\n“賢”始见于西周金文\n（字形3）\n，是在假借字上加注意符造出的分化字。国有賢人，犹家之有财，故“賢”字从“貝”。战国文字或从“賢”省﹑从“户”\n（字形7）\n，寓家有賢人之意；或从“子”\n（字形9﹑11）\n，有尊賢之意；或从“力”\n（字形10﹑12）\n，取賢者多力之意。在宋元以来的一些小说戏曲刻本中，“臤”旁多简作“”\n（见《宋元以来俗字谱》44页“堅”﹑106页“緊”﹑114页“賢”﹑125页“鏗”等字）\n。新中国成立后，“臤”旁简化为“”，“貝”简化为“贝”；“賢”类推简化为“贤”。\n（冀小军）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "requested_character": "賢",
      "redirects": [],
      "explanation_english": [
        "賢 is semantic–phonetic with 貝 and 臤. 臤 is the early form of 掔 and in Shang bronzes shows a hand and eye, an image whose original intention later became obscure. Ancient writing often borrowed 臤 for 賢; 《说文·臤部》 says “臤，古文以为賢字.” Examples include 柞伯簋 and the Guodian texts “爱亲尊臤” and “臤人不在侧，是谓迷惑.” For ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, a classical use occurs in 《庄子·徐无鬼》. For ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, a classical use occurs in 《唐虞之道》. For ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, a classical use occurs in 《周礼·地官·乡大夫》. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「君将黜耆欲，掔好恶，则耳目病矣。」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「王迟赤金十反（钣）。王曰：‘小子﹑小臣，敬又臤（賢）隻（获）则取。’」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「小子﹑小臣，恭敬而射中多的可得到这些奖品。」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「臤（賢）人不在侧，是谓迷惑。」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「賢，多才也。」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「賢者，有德行者。」.",
        "《说文》 defines 賢 as “多才也,” while Zheng Xuan glosses 賢者 as those with moral conduct. The differentiated graph with 貝 may compare a state’s worthy people to a household’s wealth; Warring-States variants add 户, 子, or 力 to express related ideas. Modern 贤 simplifies both 臤 and 貝. For ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, a classical use occurs in 《小尔雅·广诂》. For ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, a classical use occurs in 《语丛四》. For ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, a classical use occurs in 《宋元以来俗字谱》. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「臤，古文以为賢字。」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「賢，多也。」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「尧舜之行，爱亲尊臤（賢）。」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「亲臤（賢）宝知（智）。」. To show ability, moral worth, and the differentiation from 臤, the text says 「兴賢者能者。」."
      ]
