    "unicode": "U+8CE6",
    "title_english": "賦 — tax, levy, grant, declare, and fu prose",
    "summary_english": "A phonetic compound from 貝 with 武 as phonetic. 賦 first concerns taxation, then both levying and granting, declaration, a poetic mode, and the rhymed fu genre.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "賦",
      "entry_form": "賦",
      "related_headwords": [
        "赋"
      ],
      "pronunciation": "",
      "bibliography": [
        "《金文编》436页",
        "《汉语字形表》246页",
        "《说文》131页",
        "《睡甲》97页",
        "《篆隶表》421页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "形声字。从貝，武声。本义是赋税。\n《广雅·释诂二》：“賦，税也。”\n《周礼·天官·太宰》：“以九賦敛财贿。”\n唐李觏《感事》：“役频农力耗，賦重女工寒。”\n也指征收赋税。\n《说文》：“賦，敛也。”\n《左传·哀公十年》：“季氏欲以田賦。”\n汉桓宽《盐铁论·非鞅》：“是以征敌伐国，攘地斥境，不賦百姓而师以赡。”\n又有颁布﹑授予之义。\n清段玉裁《说文解字注》：“敛之曰賦，班之亦曰賦。经传中凡言以物班布与人曰賦。”\n《广雅·释诂三》：“賦，布也。”\n王念孙疏证：“賦﹑布﹑敷﹑铺，并声近而义同。”\n《国语·晋语四》：“賦职任功。”\n韦昭注：“賦，授也。”\n《吕氏春秋·分职》：“出高库之兵以賦民。”\n高诱注：“賦，予也。”\n又有宣布﹑陈述之义。\n《左传·僖公二十七年》：“賦纳以言，明试以功。”\n汉王充《论衡·对作》：“或南面称师，賦奸伪之说。”\n引申指一种铺叙直陈的诗歌表现方法。\n《释名·释典艺》：“敷布其义谓之賦。”\n《周礼·春官·大师》：“教六诗：曰风，曰賦，曰比，曰兴，曰雅，曰颂。”\n南朝梁钟嵘《诗品·序》：“直书其事，寓言写物，賦也。”\n又指一种有韵的文体。\n《史记·屈原贾生列传》：“及渡湘水，为賦以吊屈原。”\n汉班固《两都賦·序》：“賦者，古诗之流也。”\n新中国成立后，“貝”简化为“贝”，“賦”类推简化为“赋”。\n（冀小军）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "requested_character": "賦",
      "redirects": [],
      "explanation_english": [
        "A phonetic compound from 貝 with 武 as phonetic. 《广雅·释诂二》：“賦，税也。” 《周礼·天官·太宰》 speaks of collecting wealth by “九賦”, and the Tang poem 《感事》 contrasts heavy 賦 with cold women’s work. As a verb it is to levy tax: 《说文》：“賦，敛也。” 《左传·哀公十年》 says “季氏欲以田賦.”",
        "Duan Yucai notes that 賦 means both collecting and distributing: what is bestowed on people is also 賦. 《广雅·释诂三》 gives “賦，布也”; 《国语·晋语四》 uses it for assigning offices, and 《吕氏春秋·分职》 for issuing weapons. It can also mean to proclaim or state. As literary terminology, 賦 is the direct expository method: 《释名·释典艺》 says “敷布其义谓之賦”, and 《周礼》 lists it among the six poetic modes. It also denotes the rhymed fu genre, as in 《史记·屈原贾生列传》 and 班固’s 《两都賦·序》. 賦 became 赋. （冀小军）",
        "The fiscal noun is shown in 《周礼·天官·太宰》：“以九賦敛财贿。” The social burden of the same tax appears in Li Gou’s 《感事》：“役频农力耗，賦重女工寒。” Levying becomes verbal in 《左传·哀公十年》：“季氏欲以田賦。” 《盐铁论·非鞅》 confirms the contrast with not taxing people: “是以征敌伐国，攘地斥境，不賦百姓而师以赡。”",
        "Giving outward is the paired extension. Duan Yucai writes in 《说文解字注》：“敛之曰賦，班之亦曰賦。经传中凡言以物班布与人曰賦。” 《广雅·释诂三》 gives “賦，布也。” and Wang Niansun explains “賦﹑布﹑敷﹑铺，并声近而义同。” Assigned work in 《国语·晋语四》 is “賦职任功。”, where Wei Zhao says “賦，授也。” 《吕氏春秋·分职》 similarly has “出高库之兵以賦民。” and Gao You glosses “賦，予也。” Duan’s contrast captures two directions of the same administrative act: authorities gather resources and also apportion resources or duties. The 《广雅》 and Wang Niansun glosses specify the distributive direction. The 晋 and 吕氏春秋 examples then show that distributing can mean assigning an office or issuing weapons, so the verb concerns official allocation as well as taxation.",
        "The declarative sense follows from formally setting out what is assigned. 《左传·僖公二十七年》 says “賦纳以言，明试以功。” Wang Chong’s 《论衡·对作》 uses it for stating a deceptive doctrine: “或南面称师，賦奸伪之说。”",
        "As a poetic method, 《释名·释典艺》 defines it as “敷布其义谓之賦。” 《周礼·春官·大师》 lists the six modes: “教六诗：曰风，曰賦，曰比，曰兴，曰雅，曰颂。” Zhong Rong’s 《诗品·序》 clarifies the method: “直书其事，寓言写物，賦也。” 《释名》 defines the method by spreading out meaning. The 《周礼》 sequence places it beside five other recognized poetic procedures. Zhong Rong’s sentence then identifies its practical effect: events are narrated directly and objects are represented through explicit statement, a technique distinct from comparison or evocative suggestion.",
        "The resulting literary genre is shown by 《史记·屈原贾生列传》：“及渡湘水，为賦以吊屈原。” Ban Gu’s 《两都賦·序》 explains its lineage: “賦者，古诗之流也。” These passages distinguish the genre from the earlier fiscal verb."
      ]
    },
