    "unicode": "U+96B1",
    "title_english": "隱 — concealment",
    "summary_english": "A phonetic compound from 𨸏 with 㥯 as phonetic. 隱 first means being screened from sight by a hill or barrier and then concealment in general.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "隱",
      "entry_form": "隱",
      "related_headwords": [
        "隐"
      ],
      "pronunciation": "",
      "bibliography": [
        "《战文编》947页",
        "《说文》305页",
        "《睡甲》214页",
        "《篆隶表》1038页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "形声字。\n《说文》：“隱，蔽也。从𨸏，㥯声。”\n徐灏段注笺：“隱之本义盖谓隔𨸏不相见，引申为凡隐蔽之称。”\n（周宝宏）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "requested_character": "隱",
      "redirects": [],
      "explanation_english": [
        "A phonetic compound. 《说文》：“隱，蔽也。从𨸏，㥯声。” Xu Hao’s notes explain the original image as things separated by 𨸏 and unable to see one another: “隱之本义盖谓隔𨸏不相见，引申为凡隐蔽之称。” Thus the semantic component supplies the physical barrier, while the general sense is concealment or being hidden. （周宝宏）"
      ]
    },
