    "unicode": "U+5C22",
    "title_english": "尢 — a hand excrescence, fault, and exception",
    "summary_english": "A pictograph of a hand bearing a wart or other excrescence. The physical abnormality generated the later meanings fault, blame, unusual, and outstanding.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "尢",
      "entry_form": "尢",
      "related_headwords": [],
      "pronunciation": "yòu云纽、之部；云纽、尤韵、羽求切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《甲骨文字典》1539页",
        "《金文编》962页",
        "《说文》308页",
        "《马王堆》589页",
        "《篆隶表》1050页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "象形字。象人手部长赘疣之形。\n《说文》：“异也。从乙又声。”\n徐锴曰：“乙欲出而见閡，见閡则显其尤异也。”\n戴蕃豫《殷契亡尤说》认为：“象手欲上伸而碍于一”，朱芳圃《殷墟文字释丛》则认为指“赘疣”。按：戴氏﹑朱氏之说均指向了“人手”这一基本词义来源，而以朱氏之说更为可靠。字形当以“又”字为形，“又”是人手的象形字，在此基础上附加一笔表示手上所生赘疣。此义虽为本义，但并不如引申诸义项常用，后来为其专造“疣”字。而赘疣为病态，故引申出过失﹑罪过等义。《玉篇·乙部》：“尤，过也。”\n《诗·小雅·四月》：“废为残贼，莫知其尤。”\n同时手上赘疣形状突出﹑怪异，故又引申为特异﹑突出之义。此《说文》释义所由来。\n《左传·昭公二十八年》：“夫有尤物，足以移人。”\n杜预注：“尤，异也。”\n（王颖）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "requested_character": "尤",
      "redirects": [
        {
          "from": "尤",
          "to": "尢",
          "kind": "see-also"
        }
      ],
      "explanation_english": [
        "尢 is a pictograph of an excrescence on a human hand. 《说文》 gives “异也。从乙又声。”, and Xu Kai explains the shape by “乙欲出而见閡，见閡则显其尤异也。” Dai Fanyu’s 《殷契亡尤说》 reads it as a hand trying to extend against an obstruction—“象手欲上伸而碍于一”—while Zhu Fangpu’s 《殷墟文字释丛》 identifies the mark as a wart. Both interpretations recognize the hand as the graphic basis; Zhu’s account is more persuasive because 又 is the pictograph of a hand and the added stroke can directly mark a wart growing on it.",
        "This bodily sense later received the specialized graph 疣. Because a wart is a pathological irregularity, 尢 developed the meanings fault and blame. 《玉篇·乙部》 defines 尤 as “尤，过也。”, and 《诗·小雅·四月》 says “废为残贼，莫知其尤。” The conspicuous, strange shape of an excrescence also yielded ‘exceptional’ and ‘outstanding’, the source of the 《说文》 definition. 《左传·昭公二十八年》 says “夫有尤物，足以移人。”, where Du Yu glosses 尤 as “尤，异也。”"
      ]
    },
